Business Requirements Document (BRD) — Customer Service Agent
1. Document control
Project name: Customer Service Agent (CRM-aware)
Version: 1.0
Date: 2026-03-18
Owner: Customer Support / Operations
2. Background / business need
Customer support performance is impacted because the customer context required to respond to inquiries and resolve issues is not readily available during support interactions, resulting in slower responses and inconsistent handling. The business requires a Customer Service Agent that can handle customer inquiries, retrieve relevant customer information from the CRM, and support issue resolution consistently and efficiently.
3. Problem statement
Support teams need a reliable way to handle inbound customer inquiries with timely access to CRM context so issues can be resolved faster and responses remain consistent across agents and interactions.
4. Goals and objectives (measured by KPIs)
Improve First Response Time (FRT) for customer inquiries.
Improve Time to Resolution (TTR) and/or Average Handle Time (AHT) through CRM-informed handling.
Improve response consistency/quality (e.g., QA score and/or customer satisfaction measures).
5. Scope
In scope
Handle customer inquiries.
Access CRM to retrieve relevant customer/account information needed to address the inquiry.
Support issue resolution.
Out of scope
Any functionality beyond handling inquiries, CRM access, and issue resolution (not specified).
6. Stakeholders
Primary users: Customer support agents / support team
Business stakeholders: Support operations leadership
System stakeholders: CRM owners/administrators
7. Functional requirements
FR-1: Handle customer inquiries
The system shall support responding to customer inquiries.
FR-2: Access CRM
The system shall retrieve relevant customer/account information from the CRM to support inquiry handling.
FR-3: Support issue resolution
The system shall support moving the interaction toward resolving the customer’s issue.
8. Non-functional requirements (high level)
NFR-1: Reliability
The system shall be available to support inquiry handling during support operations.
NFR-2: Performance
CRM information retrieval shall be timely enough to support live inquiry handling.
NFR-3: Security and access control
CRM access shall follow existing permissioning and data access policies.
9. Success metrics / acceptance criteria
Problem clarity
The business problem and scope are documented and understood by stakeholders.
Objective relevance
KPIs used to evaluate success include FRT, TTR/AHT, and a quality/consistency metric (QA and/or satisfaction measure).
Scope definition
Delivered functionality is limited to: handle inquiries, access CRM, support issue resolution.
10. Assumptions and dependencies
Assumptions
CRM contains the customer/account information needed for inquiry handling and resolution support.
Dependencies
Access to CRM (credentials/permissions, connectivity, and required data fields availability).